{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויקם משה את המשכן", :translit "vayakem moshe et ha-mishkan", :gloss "and Moses set up the Mishkan"} {:he "משכן לא נאמר אלא המשכן", :translit "mishkan lo ne'eman ela ha-mishkan", :gloss "Mishkan was not said but the Mishkan"} {:he "לרבות משכן של מעלה", :translit "lerabot mishkan shel ma'alah", :gloss "to include the Mishkan of above"} {:he "דאיתא בפסיקתא", :translit "de-ita be-pesikta", :gloss "as it is taught in Pesikta"} {:he "שצוה הקב\"ה למלאכים של מעלה להקים משכן למעלה", :translit "she-tzivah ha-kadosh baruch hu le-malakhim shel ma'alah le-hakim mishkan le-ma'alah", :gloss "that the Holy One blessed be He commanded the angels above to set up a Mishkan on high"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Definite article 'ha-' on ha-mishkan read as inclusive ribui, extending the verse's scope to a heavenly Mishkan"}], :frame {:text "The hermeneutical principle of ribui treats the definite article 'ha-' before a noun as an extension marker, broadening its reference beyond the immediate object. Here the article on ha-mishkan is read to include a celestial counterpart, which Pesikta describes as a heavenly Mishkan that God commanded angels to construct.", :sources ["Pesikta"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Definite article 'ha-' on ha-mishkan read as inclusive ribui, extending the verse's scope to a heavenly Mishkan", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:21:33.674931861Z", :model "glm-5.2"}